# Security paths: packages that take untrusted input. A pull request that touches one gets a
# security review before the developer signs off. A package joins when its contract has an
# "Untrusted input" section, in the same pull request as that contract. One pattern a line, a
# shell glob that is also a git pathspec.
internal/telnet/*
internal/telnets/*
internal/listener/*
internal/session/*
internal/textio/*
internal/ssh/*
internal/database/*
internal/language/*
internal/bootstrap/*
internal/servicemanager/*
